# Compiled binaries. Every one of them is rebuilt by `make`.
bin/

# The simulated ABM output, 229 MB of .Rdata, and the five-variable .npz
# archives derived from it. Neither belongs in version control; see the README
# for where the .Rdata comes from and which target rebuilds the archives.
dataset/simulated/
dataset/abm_system/

# The 21,600 cached fits, 91 MB, and the manifest summarising them, 2 MB. Both
# are regenerated by `make app-abm_system_fit_qvarma`, which resumes from
# whatever is already on disk rather than refitting it.
out/abm_system_fit_qvarma/
out/abm_system_fit_qvarma_manifest.txt
out/abm_system_fit_qvarma.log

# The copy of those fits kept from before the resume logic existed, 86 MB in
# 21,600 files, and its own 2 MB manifest. Both are snapshots of a run, not
# results, and `make app-abm_system_fit_qvarma` produces the current ones.
out/abm_system_fit_qvarma_before_resume/
out/abm_system_fit_qvarma_manifest_before_resume.txt

# Everything else under out/ is small, human-readable and worth keeping: the
# fitted parameters on the real data, the loss table, the confidence set and
# the figures.

*.o
*.so
*.a
core
vgcore.*
.claude/
.DS_Store

# The 500 x 1000 throughput dataset, about 21 GB of CSV, and the 500,000 fits
# and 45 MB manifest the throughput test writes from it. Both are regenerated
# by `make app-abm_system_scale_extract` and
# `make app-abm_system_scale_fit_qvarma`. The timing file those runs produce,
# out/abm_system_scale_fit_qvarma_timing.txt, is the result and is kept.
dataset/abm_system_scale/
out/abm_system_scale_fit_qvarma_i*/
out/abm_system_scale_fit_qvarma_i*_manifest.txt
out/abm_system_scale_extract_manifest.txt
out/abm_system_scale_iteration_comparison_i*.csv

*.Rmd

# dataset/Dati simulati.zip, 226 MB: the archive dataset/simulated/ was
# unpacked from. The unpacked form is already ignored above and the README
# says where it comes from.
*.zip